### Master data: items, customers and vendors from the mock of Business Central. Every
### answer says so in meta.mock. Read-only: Business Central stays the system of record.
### Sign in first (see auth.http): REST Client keeps the cookies.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Sign in as Finance, who sees bank details, cost and prices.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/demo-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "FINANCE" }

### What the filters can offer.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/filters

### Items, a page at a time. Sort by no, description, brand, inventory,
### qtyOnSalesOrder, qtyOnPurchOrder, availableStock or unitPrice.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/items?page=1&pageSize=25&sort=availableStock&direction=asc

### Search covers the number, the description and the part number, and the
### vendor: its number, its name and its own item number.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/items?search=monitor
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/items?search=V-0002

### Filters: brand, category (COMPONENTS, PERIPHERALS, PCS,
### ENTERPRISE, SECURITY, NETWORKING), vendor and
### availability (short, low, ok).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/items?availability=short
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/items?category=SECURITY&vendor=V-0002

### One item: stock, open orders, open purchase orders and SPRs.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/items/I-0004

### An unknown number answers the 404 envelope.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/items/I-9999

### Customers: search, country and payment terms. Search also finds by the
### country's name, and by its code when the whole search is the code.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/customers?country=IN&sort=overdueOrders&direction=desc
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/customers?search=Sri%20Lanka
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/customers?paymentTerms=30%20DAYS&country=MV

### One customer: key facts, open orders and overdue orders.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/customers/C-0001

### What a customer last paid for each item asked for (at most 200, comma-separated).
### An item they never bought is left out, a bad format is a 400 and an unknown
### customer a 404. The price is masked like an item's Unit Price: sign in as
### WAREHOUSE and it answers masked: true, value: null and the reason.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/customers/C-0001/last-prices?itemNos=I-0001,I-0002

### Vendors.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/vendors?sort=balanceLcy&direction=desc

### One vendor. Finance sees the bank account. Sign in as WAREHOUSE and the same
### request answers masked: true, value: null and the reason.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/vendors/V-0001

### The available stock of many items at once (at most 200, comma-separated), for
### the lines of an order. It is the figure an item's own page gives, with no band.
### An unknown number is left out; a bad format or too many numbers is a 400.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/master-data/available-stock?itemNos=I-0001,I-0002
